y *on top* of the fact that the room you're sitting in might actually be a couple of degrees below what the thermostat says. You can test this with a cheap thermometer: you might be surprised to find your room at 69°F while the hallway reads 72°F. But even if you could magically force every room to be exactly 72°F, the radiant and humidity effects would still make it feel cooler in winter. The point about uneven heating is just one layer of the overall experience.
